ery top-level expression of every\n   636\tmodule body through the new lowering on both kernels.\n   637\t\n   638\t*(c) Not covered until phase 8.* The install-child path over **newly\n533:| the C4 linked-prelude corpus by name (§6.1.4) | 8 modules, 6 linked programs | runtime through the linked harness, read-only |\n1092:| the C4 `manifest-golden` (`linked_prelude_test.cljc:229-234`, JVM golden) and every published manifest | the C4 track's test; every publisher | phase 8 | publish twice (idempotence is already asserted) and diff the manifest map against the pre-cutover one. **Final manifest shape and every affected entry**: `:yin.module/name`, `:yin.module/schema` (1), `:yin.module/exports`, `:yin.module/requires`, `:yin.module/primitives`, `:yin.module/footprint`, `:yin.module/tree` — **unchanged**; `:yin.module/contracts` — `:yin.semantic/code` `\"v3\"`→`\"v4\"`, the three others unchanged (`\"v3\"` AST, `\"b2\"`, `\"r2\"`); `:yin.module/derivations` — all three record addresses change (semantic: output A_v4; stack and register: input A_v4 and new checksum outputs); `:yin.module/index` — **new shape** `{:yin.debruijn.code <h-storage-address> :yin.debruijn.register <r-storage-address>}`, keyed by format (within a manifest A is fixed by the semantic record, so the linker §3 amendment's `[A f]` key collapses to `f`), replacing today's `{H addr R addr}` (`publish.cljc:189`); both storage addresses change (new image bytes). Each changed address recomputes from its printed record or image |\n\n(defn- renamespace-slots\n  \"One mnemonic's operand slots, carried over unchanged in shape: only the\n   attribute is moved from `:yin.code/*` into this dimension's own\n   `:yin.debruijn.code/*` namespace; the kind and order are read straight\n   off `code/vector-operand-table`, never hand-copied.\"\n  [slots]\n  (mapv (fn [[attr kind]] [(keyword \"yin.debruijn.code\" (name attr)) kind]) slots))\n\n\n\n(defn image-hash\n  \"The ONE function that computes H (S2 item 6): `jing/sha256` over the\n   descriptor hash (which already folds in the lowering-contract\n   version) concatenated with the canonical instruction vector's own\n   bytes -- pc-indexed tuples, refs already resolved to pcs, no header,\n   exact scalar bytes. `jing/sha256`, not `jing/sha256-bytes`: this\n   dimension's canonical encoding is hex text (`encode-image` returns a\n   string, via `framed`/`to-hex`), the same shape `jing/sha256` hashes\n   for `yin.vm.debruijn/dimension-hash`, so hashing the string directly\n   is the fit; `sha256-bytes` would apply to a raw byte buffer this\n   encoder never produces. H is the ONLY executable and sharing identity\n   this file computes: no projection fingerprint, no second identity.\"\n  [v]\n  (jing/sha256 (str descriptor-hash (encode-image v))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n(defn register-hash\n  \"The ONE function that computes R (design section 3): `R = sha256\n   (register-descriptor-hash || canonical-register-vector)`. Received\n   register bytes must be hashed before decoding, as B1's wire rule\n   requires -- no receive path exists in this phase, but this function's\n   own shape (bytes in, hash out, no host-value peeking) already supports\n   that later use.\"\n  [register-image]\n  (jing/sha256 (str descriptor-hash (encode-register-image register-image))))\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-10-10 18:02:08 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-11 01:02:08 Asia/Bangkok\n\nThe golden, allocator, liveness and descriptor corrections pass. Three specification inconsistencies remain, plus one stale count. No files edited or tests run.\n\n| Severity | file:line | evidence | correction |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Medium | docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.derivations.md:629 | The module observable contains only `defined-keys`, but the following text promises normalization of stored values. Keys alone cannot check those values. “Every definition” also includes definitions inside closures that loading does not execute. | Compare a normalized store map alongside halting/blocking and assert its key set separately. Describe coverage as top-level execution and closure creation; retain phase-8 coverage for invoked module bodies. |\n| Medium | docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.derivations.md:1308 | “The record’s input is that tree” contradicts §7.6: native derivation records have input A, while the semantic record has input tree. | Qualify this as the **semantic derivation record**; native records refer to A and reach the source tree through the semantic record/association. |\n| Medium | docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.derivations.md:1092 | “Both storage addresses change” is not guaranteed. Removing a descriptor row changes checksums, but descriptors are outside the stored image payload. Payload addresses change only when payloads change. | Recompute both storage addresses from their final images without requiring inequality to previous addresses. Keep descriptor-dependent checksum regeneration separate. |\n| Low | docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.derivations.md:533 | Corpus table still says six linked programs; §6.1.4 now specifies ten root programs. | Change the count to ten. |\n\n1. **H goldens — fixed; every pc recounted.** Instruction counts for rows 1–9 are respectively **8, 12, 6, 6, 12, 14, 3/9, 9, 12**. Row 7 contains two programs. The only targets are:\n   - Row 4: alternate 4, join 5.\n   - Row 5: alternate 6, join 7.\n   - Row 6: closure body 6.\n\n   All agree with the specified emitter. No old-byte comparison is required or used.\n\n2. **Actual-successor liveness and new tail golden — fixed.** Independently derived row 9:\n\n   `f→T0, g→T1, x→T2, inner-result→T3, y→T1, outer-result→T2`; peak four registers.\n\n   The inner tail call has no successors, hence `live []`. Its following layout component has `L(4)={1,2}`, which correctly does **not** determine that tail call’s live-out. The listed R image, intervals and H tail flag agree.\n\n   Two further independent derivations agree:\n   - Row 5: conditional result reuses T1; `y→T2`, outer result T3.\n   - Definition-call row: call result T3; definition result reuses T0 after operand intervals expire.\n\n3. **Lift declarations and regeneration — fixed.** Phase 8 removes both hashed lift rows, preserves version numbers under the owner ruling, and regenerates descriptor hashes and H/R checksums. Descriptor coverage survives deletion of compiler tests. The final format-keyed manifest index is coherent because A is supplied by the semantic record. Correct the storage-address assertion above.\n\n   **Hash ruling:** `jing/sha256(dc/encode-scalar descriptor)` is exactly the existing descriptor-hash computation: stack at `debruijn_code.cljc:542-548`, register at `debruijn_register_code.cljc:257-258`. It introduces no new hash use or executable identity. A continues using Jing’s default address mechanism.\n\n4. **Import/C4 gates — largely fixed.** The ten root programs and pinned outcomes match the import tests. Eight module-root runs are separately identified, and newly published install-child coverage is explicitly gated at phase 8. Correct the module observable and coverage wording above. The module fixtures’ placeholders support their expected definition-key set